{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-09-30T16:29:41.697Z","sessionId":"5aabd1a9-14a6-4a3d-8122-b998ac8c6f10","content":"Review the conversation context below and respond with a concise summary\nof important items that should be preserved in the daily log.\nDo NOT use any tools — just return plain text.\n\nFormat your response as a structured daily log entry with these sections:\n\n**Context:** [One line about what the user was working on]\n\n**Key Exchanges:**\n- [Important Q&A or discussions]\n\n**Decisions Made:**\n- [Any decisions with rationale]\n\n**Lessons Learned:**\n- [Gotchas, patterns, or insights discovered]\n\n**Action Items:**\n- [Follow-ups or TODOs mentioned]\n\nSkip anything that is:\n- Routine tool calls or file reads\n- Content that's trivial or obvious\n- Trivial back-and-forth or clarification exchanges\n\nOnly include sections that have actual content. If nothing is worth saving,\nrespond with exactly: FLUSH_OK\n\n## Conversation Context\n\n**Assistant:** Only 2 repos have changes. Checking them, the root repo, and GitHub repos with no local folder.\n\n**Assistant:** `Linda_Projects` is not missing. It is the `Linda Projects` folder (space in the name). Committing the 2 dirty repos now.\n\n**Assistant:** Sync is done. Now finding which repo to pick up.\n\n**Assistant:** Newest real work is Flint (9/27). Windows also left a Force Plate handoff (9/28). Reading Flint status.\n\n**Assistant:** ## Sync done. The Mac is clean.\n\n**Root:** `/Users/kristinarash/DEV`\n\n**Config repos:**\n- `~/.claude`: pulled 3 commits. My commit also recorded 50 old session logs that Claude Code cleans up by itself. Git history still has them.\n- `global-memory`: pulled 3 commits from Windows. The newest is a handoff: `2026-09-28-force-plate-practitioner-closeout.md`.\n  - One log file had a conflict: `transcripts/2026-09-28.md`. I kept the lines from both machines.\n- `skills`: no new commits. The Codex sync ran.\n- **Memory mirror:** 15 projects paired. 0 files copied. 1 file replaced by a newer Mac copy. 1 index merged. Committed and pushed.\n\n**DEV repos:**\n- I checked 143 repos. 27 are active. The other 116 are dormant and clean.\n- `CommandCentre` and `graphify-out` had changes that the scheduled jobs made. I committed and pushed them.\n- I did not pull, clone, or create any repos.\n- I made no `.from-*` files.\n- `Linda_Projects` shows on GitHub with no local folder. This is not a problem. It is the local `Linda Projects` folder (the name has a space).\n\n**New hook errors since the last session:**\n- `vald-pull` failed on 9/28. Log: `~/DEV/ForcePlate_DecisionSystem/logs/last_run.json`\n- stack-doctor on 9/28 said `SecondBrain` is behind GitHub. dev-sync does not pull SecondBrain.\n- The `perch-pull` failures from 9/26 and 9/27 are still not looked at.\n\n---\n\n```\nPicking up: Flint (newest real work; still below the \"active\" cutoff)\nLast session: 2026-09-27, mac\nWhere things stand: 269 entries from 6 books are in the vault and indexed. Supertraining is done through Ch3, and the next start point is Ch4.\nBlocked on: nothing. Zatsiorsky OCR and CVASPS transcription stopped because memory was low. Restart them one at a time.\nNext: Supertraining Ch4-9, then Bondarchuk Ch3. Or first add your Issurin annotation to the vault.\n```\n\nTwo notes:\n- Item 2 in STATUS is out of date. The `step1-triage` PR was merged on 9/27.\n- Windows also left one Mac check: does `Zotero_PDFs` exist on Drive? I checked. It exists and has 301 files.\n\n**What do you want to do?** You have two options:\n1. **Flint:** continue with Supertraining Ch4.\n2. **Fix the failed jobs:** `vald-pull` and `perch-pull`. These are the Mac's data pulls. The Mac is the only machine that runs them, so nothing else gets that data.\n\nI recommend option 2. These pulls feed your force plate and GPS data. They have failed for 3 days. Flint can wait.\n\n**User:** how do we fix the hook errors?\n\n**Assistant:** Let me look at the logs first.\n\n**Assistant:** Perch is fixed already. It ran OK on 9/28. VALD failed, but its data is current to 9/28. Looking deeper.\n\n**Assistant:** VALD failed because the Mac was asleep. There was no internet, so it could not find the VALD server. This is not a code bug. Now the other errors.\n\n**Assistant:** SecondBrain and the \"behind\" repos are now up to date. The real open fix is the backup list. Let me see how a repo is listed.\n\n**Assistant:** The fix is clear. `class` does nothing in the code, and new entries use `[\"ssd\",\"github\"]`. Adding the 3 missing repos.\n\n**Assistant:** The diff is too big. My write changed the file's spacing. Fixing that so only 3 entries change.\n\n**Assistant:** Blocked, and fairly so. I will keep the backup file, like the older ones.\n\n**Assistant:** Clean diff: 3 entries only. Now I will check that the backup health check passes.\n\n**Assistant:** Same check in Python instead.\n\n**Assistant:** Backup check now passes: 0 unmanaged folders. Committing that.\n\n**Assistant:** Now I will run the VALD pull once to prove it works when the Mac is awake.\n\n**Assistant:** While VALD runs, I will check the memory compiler backlog.\n\n**Assistant:** Flush works again today. Checking whether any daily logs are still not compiled.\n\n**Assistant:** 4 logs wait. Today's log compiles tonight. I will compile the 3 older ones now, in the background.\n\n**Assistant:** Two jobs are running now. I will report when both finish.\n\n<br>\n\n**Assistant:** VALD works. It ran OK on the first try. Now I wait for the compiler.\n\n**Assistant:** The 9/27 log failed. Finding out why.\n\n**Assistant:** All done. Here is the result.\n\n## What I fixed\n\n**1. VALD pull: fixed.**\n- Cause: on 9/28 the Mac was asleep, so it had no internet and could not reach VALD.\n- This was not a code bug.\n- I ran it again now. It worked on the first try. The data is current to 9/28.\n\n**2. Perch pull: nothing to fix.**\n- It worked by itself on 9/28. The data is current to 9/28.\n\n**3. Backup \"unmanaged\" error: fixed.**\n- 3 repos were not in the backup list: `Flint`, `RunningTheRoom`, `AI_Analyst`.\n- I added them to `~/.claude/scripts/backup-manifest.json`. I checked the file again after the change, and 0 folders are missing now.\n- Committed and pushed as `fd10769`.\n\n**4. \"Repo behind\" errors (SecondBrain, global-memory, skills): fixed.**\n- Today's sync brought all three up to date.\n\n**5. Memory compiler backlog: mostly fixed.**\n- I compiled 9/16 and 9/19. The knowledge base grew from 301 to 309 articles. Cost: about $2.70.\n- Today's log (9/29) will compile tonight.\n- The 9/27 log did not compile. It has no session notes, only the error line from the 9/27 \"session limit\" failure, so nothing is lost. Your Flint work from that day is saved in `Flint/docs/STATUS.md` and its handoff.\n\n## What you do now\n\nNothing. The old lines stay in `.errors.log` because it is a history log. From tomorrow you should see no new lines for these problems.\n\nOne small follow-up: the Mac sleeps through some scheduled jobs. If a job fails with \"Failed to resolve\", it slept. Run the job again, and it will work.\n\n**User:** are the Database pulls up to date?\n\n**Assistant:** Checking all three Mac pulls: GPS, Perch, and VALD.\n\n**Assistant:** GPS pull is running right now. Finding its log.\n\n**Assistant:** GPS is mid-run (started 10:00). Let me see what the 9/28 run found, and wait for this one.\n\n**Assistant:** It found 1 new session and is importing it now. Waiting for it to finish.\n\n**Assistant:** Yes. All three database pulls are up to date to yesterday (9/28).\n\n| Pull | Last run | Result | Newest data |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| GPS | Today 10:04 | OK | 9/28 practice (added just now) |\n| VALD | Today 09:39 | OK | 9/28 |\n| Perch | Yesterday 16:39 | OK | 9/28 |\n\nNotes:\n- The GPS run ended 1 minute ago. It added 1 new session: the 9/28 practice. Catapult was slow once, but the retry worked.\n- There is no 9/29 data yet in any database. That is normal, because today's sessions are not done.\n- The afternoon runs will pull today's data.\n\nYou do not have to do anything."}
